==German==

===Etymology===
16th century, from archaic {{suffix|de|stochen|t1=to stir, stoke|-ern|pos2=frequentative suffix}}. Said verb is derived from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*stokōn}} (whence {{cog|en|stoke}}), possibly through {{der|de|gml|stōken}}. See {{m|de|stochen}} for more. Ultimately related with {{m|de|stoßen|t=to thrust}} and {{m|de|Stock|t=stick}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtɔxəʁn/|[ˈʃtɔ.χɐn]}}
* {{audio|de|De-stochern.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# to [[poke]], [[pick]]
#: {{ux|de|Er '''stocherte''' lustlos in seinem Essen herum.|He '''poked''' around halfheartedly in his food.}}

